For integer polynomials, $a-b\mid f(a)-f(b)$. With $f(n)=n^2-4n-18$:
* $n-1\mid f(n)-f(1)=n^2-4n-17=(n-1)(n-3)-20$, so $n-1\mid20$;
* $n-4\mid f(n)-2=n^2-4n-20=n(n-4)-20$, so $n-4\mid20$;
* $n-8\mid f(n)-34=n^2-4n-52=(n-8)(n+4)-20$, so $n-8\mid20$.

$n-1\mid20$ gives $n\in\{-19,-9,-4,-3,-1,0,2,3,5,6,11,21\}$. Of these, $n-4\mid 20$ leaves $n\in\{-1,0,2,3,5,6\}$, and $n-8\mid 20$ leaves $n\in\{3,6\}$ (e.g. $n=0$: $-8\nmid20$; $n=2$: $-6\nmid 20$; $n=5$: $-3\nmid20$; $n=-1$: $-9\nmid20$). Both are attained by the examples in the first solution. **Answer: $3$ and $6$.**
